        {
            "id": "TASK-014",
            "title": "Implement Task Editing and Dependency-Based Status Validation",
            "description": "Add task editing functionality to the detail modal. Allow users to update the title, description, priority, size, deadline and status. Validate edited values against the task model before saving. Implement the dependency business rule: a task cannot be moved to Done while any of its dependencies remains in a status other than Done. Display a clear explanation when the rule prevents a status change. Save every accepted update through the state and storage modules and refresh the corresponding task card and project statistics.",
            "userStories": [
                "As a user, I want to update task information so that I can adapt the development plan as the project evolves.",
                "As a user, I want task dependencies to be enforced so that dependent work cannot be marked Done prematurely.",
                "As a user, I want my manual changes to persist after reloading the page so that my task updates are not lost."
            ],
            "acceptanceCriteria": [
                "The user can edit the title, description, priority, size, deadline and status.",
                "Priority, size and status accept only their permitted values.",
                "The edited deadline remains within the project duration and follows the Day N format.",
                "A task can be marked Done only when all its dependencies have status Done.",
                "An attempted invalid transition to Done is rejected.",
                "A clear message identifies that unfinished dependencies prevent completion.",
